_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The spec is implemented, and the check passes: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n 4 tests/config --ignore=tests/config/cli/test_argcomplete.py` gives 7037 passed, 2 skipped. I re-ran it myself after the implementer finished. I didn't read the diff line by line, so the review was limited to confirming that only the six files named in the spec changed and that no test files were touched.\n\nThe implementer departed from the spec in two places:\n- **Emptied base:** when a factor filter empties the base `set_env` (`win: MAGIC=base` on Linux), the base now becomes `\"\"` and the appended override still applies. The spec's general \"a `KeyError` gives `\"\"`\" wording would otherwise have blocked this.\n- **`KeyError` scope:** `_resolve_section_proxy` now catches `KeyError` only around `process_raw`, not around the reference resolution.\n\nNot checked:\n- ruff isn't installed in the venv, so the changes weren't linted.\n- Running the wider `tests` directory gave 4 failures and 7 errors. The implementer attributes them to the environment (`tombi` missing, an argcomplete attribute missing, package metadata for `test_version.py`). It didn't confirm they also fail on the base commit.", "ttft_ms": 2136, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 24187, "uuid": "b0f73127-8fdb-4e64-8de9-6cf8bd905a37", "ttft_stream_ms": 1607, "time_to_request_ms": 19, "first_content_frame_ms": 1607, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
